## Scope

This file is the project-wide default. Two areas carry their own, more
specific terms:

- **`datasets/gold/`** — see [`datasets/gold/LICENSE.md`](datasets/gold/LICENSE.md).
  Same license (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) from 2026-08-12 forward, but with an
  irrevocable historical exception: `gold_v1.0` through `gold_v1.2.3` were
  published under CC-BY-4.0 before this project-wide decision existed, and
  that grant cannot be revoked — see that file and
  [PDR-006](docs/decisions/PDR-006.md) for the full detail. Nothing else in
  this repository has a comparable prior grant to account for.
- **`datasets/real_validation.jsonl`** and **`datasets/real_holdout.jsonl`**
  — not licensed at all; excluded from version control, contain the
  project owner's real personal notes, never published (see
  [PDR-004](docs/decisions/PDR-004.md)).

## Model weights

Released model weights (`intent-recovery-model-*` GitHub Releases) carry
this same license. The base model, `google/flan-t5-base`, is Apache 2.0 —
a permissive license that does not require derivative works (including
fine-tuned weights) to remain Apache 2.0 (Apache 2.0 §4: a licensee "may
provide additional or different license terms... for any such Derivative
Works"). Google's own Apache 2.0 notice for `flan-t5-base` is unaffected
and not superseded by this file.

## Why not "open source"

A NonCommercial restriction is incompatible with the Open Source
Initiative's Open Source Definition (criterion 6: no discrimination
against fields of endeavor). This project is precisely described as
**source-available/noncommercial**, not OSI "open source" — even though
"open source" is how the product owner describes it in plain language
elsewhere. See [PDR-006](docs/decisions/PDR-006.md) and
[PDR-007](docs/decisions/PDR-007.md) for the full reasoning.

## GitHub license detection

GitHub's automatic license detector has a known gap identifying
CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 even from a root-level file like this one
(`licensee/licensee#343`). This file's text is what legally governs
regardless of whether the repository sidebar badge recognizes it.
